{"title":"Nuclear Bomb Physics","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Nuclear_Bomb_Physics\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Nuclear Bomb Physics</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Fundamental_Concepts\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Fundamental Concepts</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Energy_from_Fission\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Energy from Fission</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Chain_Reaction_Growth\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Chain Reaction Growth</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Critical_and_Supercritical_Mass\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Critical and Supercritical Mass</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Assembly_Methods\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Assembly Methods</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Fusion_Boosting_and_Thermonuclear_Stages\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Fusion Boosting and Thermonuclear Stages</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Neutron_Diffusion_and_Leakage\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Neutron Diffusion and Leakage</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Time_Scale_of_Explosion\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Time Scale of Explosion</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Yield_Estimates\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Yield Estimates</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Nuclear_Bomb_Physics\">Nuclear Bomb Physics</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nuclear_Bomb_Physics&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Nuclear Bomb Physics\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><b>Nuclear bomb physics</b> deals with the principles, mathematics, and engineering behind nuclear weapons, which unleash enormous energy by triggering extremely rapid, uncontrolled nuclear chain reactions. These bombs rely primarily on nuclear <b>fission</b> and <b>fusion</b> to release energy measured in kilotons to megatons of TNT equivalent.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Fundamental_Concepts\">Fundamental Concepts</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nuclear_Bomb_Physics&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Fundamental Concepts\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Energy_from_Fission\">Energy from Fission</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nuclear_Bomb_Physics&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Energy from Fission\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Each fission event of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/c/77c2903ae65ae24283c89363c5a635149ee50d3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${}^{235}U$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"17\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/e/7feeac4795e16f88cc3a42eb8c5dafb7ff3c0dab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${}^{239}Pu$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"17\" /> releases about 200 MeV of energy:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/e/a0ea1d405048936156d9ef87756cf12c94d387da.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[E_{fission} \\approx 200 \\text{ MeV} = 3.2 \\times 10^{-11} \\text{ J}\\]\" width=\"276\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/8/0b8e50b09cbf2bc5c3193f6c664b1799c826dc01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N_f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"25\" height=\"19\" /> nuclei undergo fission, total energy released is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63fd6616b42262f700039ee68cf048a09adae215.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[E_{total} = N_f \\times E_{fission}\\]\" width=\"169\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>For example, 1 gram of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/c/77c2903ae65ae24283c89363c5a635149ee50d3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${}^{235}U$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"17\" /> contains approximately\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/9/b59c2ac08ef50ca13fdd1cb62b72b2162a40efbf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[N = \\frac{6.022 \\times 10^{23}}{235} \\approx 2.56 \\times 10^{21} \\text{ atoms}\\]\" width=\"300\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>If 1% fissions:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/9/bc9f527d69a09239f4929c9841e00ab52244b096.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[E = 0.01 \\times N \\times 3.2 \\times 10^{-11} \\approx 8.2 \\times 10^{8} \\text{ J}\\]\" width=\"328\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>This is equivalent to about 200 tons of TNT (1 ton TNT = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/7/727815210108fde0b2e85c251c4b131deda8b24e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4.184 \\times 10^{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"91\" height=\"18\" /> J).\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Chain_Reaction_Growth\">Chain Reaction Growth</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nuclear_Bomb_Physics&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Chain Reaction Growth\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The number of neutrons (and fissions) grows exponentially during detonation:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/b/aeb6c023d6dcf814bb8ef8c71b766c98ac94cb65.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[N(t) = N_0 e^{\\alpha t}\\]\" width=\"105\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> is the neutron population growth rate, related to neutron generation time <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/2/2d295c3b71504a216422e5fffdfbad742c7add64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Lambda$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> and multiplication factor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> by:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/0/fa05de248e380f08c04369f379aaad2b937e642d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\alpha = \\frac{k - 1}{\\Lambda}\\]\" width=\"78\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Typical neutron generation time <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/2/2d295c3b71504a216422e5fffdfbad742c7add64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Lambda$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> in a bomb core is on the order of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/6/726ccb1c5b1dd30ff6544e6a48732f1caa842856.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{-8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"17\" /> seconds, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> can be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/5/0a5b7e9c297d5ee6dce5d1b385443c232bd4414b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&gt;2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> can be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/1/47175373a119092909167d80227a036d3b364d88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sim 10^{8} \\text{ s}^{-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"77\" height=\"17\" />, meaning neutron numbers can double every nanosecond.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Critical_and_Supercritical_Mass\">Critical and Supercritical Mass</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nuclear_Bomb_Physics&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Critical and Supercritical Mass\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The <b>critical mass</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/0/480cc240e9da5bb0b22a7038358266e748c4d0ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M_c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> is the minimum fissile material mass for sustaining a chain reaction:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/d/81d3e569893c3b05d258cf15e6e089b6d3986dce.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k = 1 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad \\text{steady neutron population}\\]\" width=\"296\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Above critical mass, the system becomes supercritical (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/1/411e8b2b30fbb26e55ed0d28303d10fa81aa5606.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />) and reaction grows explosively.\n</p><p>The multiplication factor depends on geometry, density <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/2/0027034d8a10372a06deaf4f4084c01956587479.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\rho$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"9\" height=\"11\" />, neutron reflection, and fissile purity:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/c/70c3e1358334b97e0b044f5c3dd31b65ea3c2a03.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k = \\eta f p \\epsilon \\times \\text{(geometry factor)}\\]\" width=\"219\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Increasing density via implosion reduces critical mass:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/0/a307140969819aa3b0d88a31dde3ea05c1ed929f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[M_c \\propto \\frac{1}{\\rho^2}\\]\" width=\"67\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Assembly_Methods\">Assembly Methods</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nuclear_Bomb_Physics&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Assembly Methods\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><b>Gun-type assembly</b>: Rapidly shoots one subcritical mass into another, forming a supercritical assembly. This method requires less precision but can only be used with uranium-235 due to spontaneous fission constraints.\n</p><p><b>Implosion-type assembly</b>: Uses shaped conventional explosives to symmetrically compress a subcritical plutonium or uranium core, increasing density and making it supercritical. The compression factor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> increases density:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/4/9e4c88173fb36bdda271199606a9d6b35fbd9188.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\rho_{compressed} = C \\times \\rho_0,\\]\" width=\"161\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>reducing critical mass by\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/2/9c2e163b32edf4b5a636c075984e58c6d6762008.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[M_c \\propto \\frac{1}{C^2}.\\]\" width=\"77\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Fusion_Boosting_and_Thermonuclear_Stages\">Fusion Boosting and Thermonuclear Stages</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nuclear_Bomb_Physics&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Fusion Boosting and Thermonuclear Stages\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Fusion reactions add tremendous yield:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/e/c7e7e8b3f9dd4f2dc553266ca314ee1c58bcea33.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[{}^{2}H + {}^{3}H \\rightarrow {}^{4}He + n + 17.6 \\text{ MeV}\\]\" width=\"258\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Neutrons from fusion can cause additional fission in a uranium tamper:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/f/87f8e1d976cdffa9463a75030eed85f23eee8950.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[E_{fusion} \\sim 10 \\times E_{fission} \\text{ per reaction chain}\\]\" width=\"315\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Neutron_Diffusion_and_Leakage\">Neutron Diffusion and Leakage</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nuclear_Bomb_Physics&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Neutron Diffusion and Leakage\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Neutron leakage reduces efficiency. The neutron diffusion length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> affects neutron retention:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/e/cce8e26a93f606ae2d42753a6c04b7a0f2ccbde5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[L = \\sqrt{\\frac{D}{\\Sigma_a}},\\]\" width=\"83\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>where\n</p>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> = diffusion coefficient,</li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/f/daf7c88c757e88a3cfb3bdde65e549ea70bbb938.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Sigma_a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> = macroscopic absorption cross-section.</li></ul>\n<p>Optimizing geometry minimizes leakage and maximizes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Time_Scale_of_Explosion\">Time Scale of Explosion</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nuclear_Bomb_Physics&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Time Scale of Explosion\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>With neutron generation time <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/5/1a54ff8a959c66a3abc04526d2ef79dbda2cce31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Lambda \\approx 10^{-8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"75\" height=\"17\" /> s and initial neutrons <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/e/4eea9ffe81b4ccfb2ebe3b3bdb6260d7c2c2458f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N_0 \\sim 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"17\" />, after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> generations over time <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/c/91c7c1956cff90aeb46e181bb9a886067faa9bc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = n \\Lambda$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/2/f32a6a286a5d77478ade06996ffb80460e1b2acc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[N(t) = e^{\\alpha t} = 2^{t / t_d}\\]\" width=\"140\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>where doubling time\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/d/0fdd72651d3dec63ac58d9b3ec4fa9c405458aca.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[t_d = \\frac{\\ln 2}{\\alpha} \\sim 10^{-9} \\text{ s}.\\]\" width=\"145\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>The chain reaction completes in microseconds, releasing energy almost instantaneously.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Yield_Estimates\">Yield Estimates</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nuclear_Bomb_Physics&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Yield Estimates\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Energy yield <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> in kilotons of TNT:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/a/4aac3412039af1e8043e02ab9008085a3cf4305e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[Y \\text{ (kt)} = \\frac{E_{total}}{4.184 \\times 10^{12} \\text{ J/kt}}\\]\" width=\"207\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>For a bomb with 10 kg of fissioned material:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/c/9fc127620b2ab01cb772aaaa7d29ffd679407d7e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[N_f = \\frac{6.022 \\times 10^{23}}{235} \\times 10 = 2.56 \\times 10^{25}\\]\" width=\"296\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Energy:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/a/fea4b0bb6753312f780b1ec97f289f7306ee3c90.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[E = N_f \\times 3.2 \\times 10^{-11} = 8.2 \\times 10^{14} \\text{ J}\\]\" width=\"287\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Yield:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/f/88f7e50b3bcfe41d6d7ed49986f2e7965eeddb2f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[Y = \\frac{8.2 \\times 10^{14}}{4.184 \\times 10^{12}} \\approx 196 \\text{ kt}\\]\" width=\"209\" height=\"39\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nuclear_Bomb_Physics&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nuclear_Fission\" title=\"Nuclear Fission\">Nuclear Fission</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nuclear_Fusion\" title=\"Nuclear Fusion\">Nuclear Fusion</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Critical_Mass&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Critical Mass (page does not exist)\">Critical Mass</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nuclear_Chain_Reaction\" title=\"Nuclear Chain Reaction\">Nuclear Chain Reaction</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nuclear_Reactor_Physics\" title=\"Nuclear Reactor Physics\">Nuclear Reactor Physics</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Hydrodynamics_of_Explosions&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Hydrodynamics of Explosions (page does not exist)\">Hydrodynamics of Explosions</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018015250\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.028 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.041 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 267/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8824/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:32678:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018015250 and revision id 251963. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}